<%#
  T-26a increment 3 — THE OWNED MY-PAGE SPENT-TIME REPORT WIDGET (FR-01).

  New in this plugin. The base plugin ships `my/blocks/_report_by_spent_time.erb` and this
  plugin only ever overrode its issue sibling, so on a standalone install this block did
  not exist at all — the last dashboard feature FR-01 was still missing. Read the long note
  in `_report_by_issues.erb` first: this file's PATH is its registration, core rescues only
  `ActionView::MissingTemplate`, and everything there about the guard applies here.

  --- ONE THING THIS ONE HAS AND THE OTHER DOES NOT ---

  `:view_time_entries`, asked GLOBALLY. The project dashboard asks it per project
  (`ReporterProjectPagesHelper#render_reporter_project_block`); here there is no project, so
  the question is whether this actor may see spent time ANYWHERE. It is asked through
  `WidgetReport.block_permitted?` rather than inline, so both surfaces read one rule.

  Refusing renders the labelled placeholder rather than nothing, for the reason the whole
  file exists: a block that renders as nothing loses its own close button.

  The base plugin's version of this file resolved its query with a bare
  `TimeEntryQuery.find_by_id` — no `visible` — so a my-page widget there could be pointed at
  somebody else's private time query by id (verified against its source, 2026-08-12). This
  one goes through `TimeEntryQuery.visible(actor)`, and the report itself through
  `TimeEntry.visible(actor)` inside `ReportScope`.
%>
<% begin %>
  <%
    block ||= 'report_by_spent_time'
    rrd_actor = User.current
    settings ||= rrd_actor.pref.my_page_settings(block)
    rrd_permitted = RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.block_permitted?(block, rrd_actor)
    rrd_widget = if rrd_permitted
                   RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.render_for_my_page(
                     actor: rrd_actor, block: block, settings: settings, logger: Rails.logger
                   )
                 end
  %>

  <% if !rrd_permitted %>
    <p class="nodata"><%= l(:label_no_data) %></p>
  <%# T-52 — THE THIRD STATE, AND THE SETTINGS FORM RENDERS UNDER IT.
      A stored project this actor may no longer read shows NO figures: the owner asked for
      one project, and a report that silently grew because a permission was withdrawn is the
      wrong way to be wrong (INV-3, CLAUDE.md §4). It is not an error placeholder either —
      nothing went wrong, the setting is simply unusable.
      The FORM is what makes it a state rather than a dead end. Core gives a my-page block
      only Move and Delete, and this partial's unresolved branch is the only place the
      settings form exists at all — so a bare notice would tell the reader to change a
      setting that was no longer on the page. Measured by an independent review: deleting
      and re-adding the block was the only way out, and
      `UserPreference#clear_unused_block_settings` throws the template and query away with
      it. %>
  <% elsif rrd_widget && !rrd_widget.project_unavailable %>
    <%= render partial: 'reporter_dashboards/widgets/my_report',
               locals: { block: block, widget: rrd_widget, user: rrd_actor } %>
  <% else %>
    <% if rrd_widget %>
      <p class="nodata"><%= l(:text_reporter_widget_project_unavailable) %></p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render partial: 'reporter_dashboards/widgets/my_report_settings',
               locals: { block: block, settings: settings, report_type: :spent_time,
                         queries: TimeEntryQuery.visible(rrd_actor).sorted,
                         report_templates: RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.templates_for(
                           project: nil, actor: rrd_actor, source: 'time_entries'
                         ),
                         projects: RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.projects_for(
                           actor: rrd_actor
                         ) } %>
  <% end %>
<% rescue StandardError, ScriptError => rrd_error %>
  <% RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.log_my_page_failure(rrd_error) %>
  <p class="nodata"><%= l(:error_reporter_widget_render_failed) %></p>
<% end %>
